:: Mansion Steal Dumb
<<set $location to "avery_mansion">><<set $avery_passage to $passage>><<set $outside to 0>><<effects>><<avery_mansion>>
<<speechresolve>>
<<set $skulduggerydifficulty to 800>>
<<if ($phase is "bottle_of_milk" and (effectiveTransformationLevel("cat") gte 6)) or ($phase is "wild_honeycomb" and (effectiveTransformationLevel("bear") gte 6)) or ($phase is "chicken_egg" and (effectiveTransformationLevel("fox") gte 6)) or ($phase is "pork" and (effectiveTransformationLevel("cow") gte 6))>>
	<<set $skulduggerydifficulty to 500>>
<</if>>
<<skulduggerycheck "silent">>
<<if $skulduggerysuccess is 1>>
	<<switch $phase>>
	<<case "banana" "wild_carrot" "chilli_pepper">>
		<<if (_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "shy" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "polite" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant")>>
			"I wanted to use <<recipe_name $phase "article">>," you say the first thing that comes to mind. "F-For pleasure."<br>
		<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel")>>
			"I wanted to fuck <<recipe_name $phase "article">>," you say the first thing that comes to mind.<br>
		<<else>>
			"I wanted to use <<recipe_name $phase "article">> as a dildo," you say the first thing that comes to mind.<br>
		<</if>>
		<br>
		<<if C.npc.Avery.penis isnot "none">>
			"Why? I'm sure I can do it better.
		<<else>>
			"Just don't put it in any food later.
		<</if>>
		<<if $avery_mansion.jobs.includes("kitchen")>>And clean this mess up.<</if>>"<<averyKitchenExit "calm">>
	<<case "bottle_of_milk">>
		<<if (effectiveTransformationLevel("cat") gte 6)>>
			You meow and drink the milk without saying a word. 
			<br><br>
			Avery raises <<his>> eyebrow, but doesn't say anything until you finish.
			"Right, you are my kitten after all.<<if $avery_mansion.jobs.includes("kitchen")>>Just clean up the mess after yourself.<</if>>"
			<br><br>
		<<else>>
			<<if (_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "shy")>>
				"I was trying to make <<recipe_name $phase2 "article">>," you explain, keeping your eyes on the mess. "I panicked when you came in."
			<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant")>>
				"I was attempting <<recipe_name $phase2 "article">>," you say, forcing a neat voice over a very untidy scene.
			<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile">>
				"I was trying to make <<recipe_name $phase2 "article">>," you say. "I'll clean it up."
			<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel")>>
				"I wanted to make <<recipe_name $phase2 "article">>," you say, leaning into the excuse before it can wobble. "The jar was badly placed."
			<<else>>
				"I wanted to make <<recipe_name $phase2 "article">>," you say, steadying yourself before Avery can pick the excuse apart.
			<</if>>
			<<if setup.foodstuff[$phase2]?.recipe>>
				If only you knew how to make it.
				<br><br>
				"<<recipe_name $phase2 "cap">>?" Avery raises <<his>> eyebrow. "I didn't know you could cook <<recipe_name $phase2 "article">>. Aren't you full of surprises? <<if $avery_mansion.jobs.includes("kitchen")>>Still, you must clean up.<<else>>Still, you should be more careful with your cooking experiments.<</if>>"
			<<else>>
				<br><br>
				"Makes sense," <<he>> answers, <<his>> curiosity satisfied. "<<if $avery_mansion.jobs.includes("kitchen")>>Just clean this up.<<else>>Just be more careful.<</if>>"
			<</if>>
		<</if>>
		<br><br>
		<<averyKitchenExit "calm">>
	<<case "apple" "orange" "lemon" "pear" "strawberry" "peach" "plum" "blackberry" "tomato">>
		<<if (_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "shy" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "polite" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant")>>
			"I wanted a snack," you say, looking at the fruit and then at the broken glass. "I should have asked first."
		<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel")>>
			"I wanted something fresh," you say, refusing to sound as guilty as the floor looks. "The jar was in the way."
		<<else>>
			"I wanted something fresh," you say. "Then I knocked the jar down."
		<</if>>
		<br><br>
		"Right, of course. <<if $avery_mansion.jobs.includes("kitchen")>>Just clean this up.<<else>>Just be more careful.<</if>>
		<br><br>
		<<averyKitchenExit "calm">>
	<<case "wild_honeycomb">>
		<<if (effectiveTransformationLevel("bear") gte 6)>>
			<<if (_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "shy" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "polite" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant")>>
				"I wanted to eat the honeycomb. With larvae and wax," you must have gotten a bit too much into the detail because Avery stopped you.<br>
			<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel")>>
				"I'm a bear<<girl>>, eating honeycombs is pretty normal for me. Wax and larvae and such," you must have gotten a bit too much into the detail because Avery stopped you.<br>
			<<else>>
				"I really like eating honeycombs. Wax and all. And the larvae," you must have gotten a bit too much into the detail because Avery stopped you.<br>
			<</if>>
			<br>
		<<else>>
			<<if (_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "shy" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "polite" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant")>>
				"I wanted to make some candles from the wax," you explain. "But I made a mess. I'm sorry."<br>
			<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel")>>
				"It was for candlemaking," you start explaining. "Honey-scented candles."<br>
			<<else>>
				"I wanted to make some candles," you explain. "From the wax."<br>
			<</if>>
			<br>
			"Candles?" Avery raises <<his>> eyebrow, slightly surprised. "I didn't know you were interested in such things. Well, just make sure it does not go to waste. They are hard to come by.<<if $avery_mansion.jobs.includes("kitchen")>> Also, clean that mess before somebody gets injured.<</if>>"
		<</if>>
		<br><br>
		<<averyKitchenExit "calm">>
	<<case "garlic_bulb">>
		<<if (_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "shy" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "polite" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant")>>
			"I think I caught a flu," you start. "I didn't want to give you a cold, so I wanted to take something healthy."<br>
		<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel")>>
			"I caught something," you start. "Thought some garlic would help."<br>
		<<else>>
			"My throat is sore," you start. "I think I caught something and I thought I'd kill it before it develops. Wouldn't want to get you sick."<br>
		<</if>>
		<br>
		"I'm sure it will help.<<if $avery_mansion.jobs.includes("kitchen")>> Just clean the glass first.<</if>>"
		<<averyKitchenExit "calm">>
	<<case "chicken_egg">>
		<<if (effectiveTransformationLevel("fox") gte 6)>>
			<<if (_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "shy" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "polite" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant")>>
				"I'm sorry, I just wanted to bury the egg," you start your explanation. "I'm a fox<<girl>>, and I really felt like I needed it."<br>
			<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel")>>
				"I'm a fox<<girl>>. I felt the need to bury an egg, so I took the egg."<br>
			<<else>>
				"I wanted to bury the egg," you start your explanation. "I'm a fox<<girl>>, it's my natural need."<br>
			<</if>>
			<br>
			Avery chuckles. "You wanted to bury it, obviously. I suppose you do look the part.
			<<if $avery_mansion.jobs.includes("kitchen")>>
				Well, you still have to clean it up, my <<= $player.gender_appearance is "m" ? "kit" : "vixen">>." <<He>> sighs. "Take that egg, just don't break anything more.
				<br>
			<<else>>
				Just leave that for the maids to clean." <<He>>  stops and then sighs. "You can take that egg, just don't break anything more.
				<br>
			<</if>>"
			<br><br>
			<<He>> leaves the kitchen.
			<<tending_pick $phase 1 1>>
		<<else>>
			<<if (_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "shy")>>
				"I was trying to make <<recipe_name $phase2 "article">>," you explain, glancing from Avery to the broken jar. "I panicked when you came in."
			<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant")>>
				"I was attempting <<recipe_name $phase2 "article">>," you say, smoothing your tone despite the state of the floor.
			<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile">>
				"I was trying to make <<recipe_name $phase2 "article">>," you say. "I'll put everything right."
			<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel")>>
				"I wanted to make <<recipe_name $phase2 "article">>," you say, grabbing the excuse before Avery can. "Your jar was in the way."
			<<else>>
				"I wanted to make <<recipe_name $phase2 "article">>," you say, keeping your answer simple enough to survive inspection.
			<</if>>
			<<if setup.foodstuff[$phase2]?.recipe>>
				If only you knew the recipe.
				<br><br>
				"<<recipe_name $phase2 "cap">>?" Avery raises <<his>> eyebrow. "I didn't know you could cook <<recipe_name $phase2 "article">>. Aren't you full of surprises? <<if $avery_mansion.jobs.includes("kitchen")>>Still, you must clean up.<<else>>Still, you should be more careful with your cooking experiments.<</if>>
			<<else>>
				<br><br>
				"Makes sense," <<he>> answers, <<his>> curiosity satisfied. <<if $avery_mansion.jobs.includes("kitchen")>>Just clean this up.<<else>>Just be more careful.<</if>>
			<</if>>
		<</if>>
		<br><br>
		<<averyKitchenExit "calm">>
	<<case "beef" "pork">>
		<<if (effectiveTransformationLevel("cow") gte 6) and $phase is "pork">>
			<<if (_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "shy" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "polite" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant")>>
				"I'm sorry. I felt really bad about it being in the fridge, and I don't know why," you say, and to make sure the point hits, you moo afterwards.<br>
			<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel")>>
				You moo lowly. More like a bull than an obedient cow. "It's fucking pork. It's basically like cannibalism for me. Had to get rid of that."<br>
			<<else>>
				"I felt bad about it being in the fridge, and I don't know why," you say, and to make sure the point hits, you moo afterwards.<br>
			<</if>>
			<br>
			Avery's gaze softens slightly. Just for a moment, it looks like <<he>> understands, or at least suspects why. It doesn't last long though. "I will overlook this one. But you can't just throw out ingredients I buy. They are in the fridge for a reason. You don't need to eat it.<<if $avery_mansion.jobs.includes("kitchen")>> And clean that up.<<else>> And be more careful.<</if>>"
			<br><br>
			<<averyKitchenExit "calm">>
		<<elseif ((effectiveTransformationLevel("wolf") gte 6) or (effectiveTransformationLevel("bird") gte 6) or (effectiveTransformationLevel("cat") gte 6) or (effectiveTransformationLevel("bear") gte 6) or (effectiveTransformationLevel("fox") gte 6))>>
			<<if (_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "shy" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "polite" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant")>>
				"I wanted some raw meat," you start your explanation. "I'm a <<if (effectiveTransformationLevel("cat") gte 6)>>cat<<girl>><<elseif (effectiveTransformationLevel("wolf") gte 6)>>wolf<<girl>><<elseif (effectiveTransformationLevel("bear") gte 6)>>bear<<girl>><<elseif (effectiveTransformationLevel("fox") gte 6)>>fox<<girl>><<elseif (effectiveTransformationLevel("bird") gte 6)>>harpy<</if>>, so I think it's just natural for me."<br>
			<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel")>>
				"I'm a <<if (effectiveTransformationLevel("cat") gte 6)>>cat<<girl>><<elseif (effectiveTransformationLevel("wolf") gte 6)>>wolf<<girl>><<elseif (effectiveTransformationLevel("bear") gte 6)>>bear<<girl>><<elseif (effectiveTransformationLevel("fox") gte 6)>>fox<<girl>><<elseif (effectiveTransformationLevel("bird") gte 6)>>harpy<</if>>, so I just took some raw meat. I'm a carnivore after all."<br>
			<<else>>
				"I craved raw meat," you start your explanation. "I'm a <<if (effectiveTransformationLevel("cat") gte 6)>>cat<<girl>><<elseif (effectiveTransformationLevel("wolf") gte 6)>>wolf<<girl>><<elseif (effectiveTransformationLevel("bear") gte 6)>>bear<<girl>><<elseif (effectiveTransformationLevel("fox") gte 6)>>fox<<girl>><<elseif (effectiveTransformationLevel("bird") gte 6)>>harpy<</if>>. The craving is not exactly polite, but it is there."<br>
			<</if>>
			<br>
			"I did ask for that explanation, didn't I? Just take it. And make sure you cook it for me properly. The last thing I need is to get sick from undercooked meat again."
			<br><br>
			<<averyKitchenExit "calm">><<if $avery_mansion.jobs.includes("kitchen")>> Avery didn't mention it, but you probably still have to clean that kitchen.<</if>> <<tending_pick $phase 2 4>>
		<<else>>
			<<if (_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "shy")>>
				"I was trying to make <<recipe_name $phase2 "article">>," you say, eyes dropping to the glass. "Then you walked in and I lost my nerve."
			<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant")>>
				"I was attempting <<recipe_name $phase2 "article">>," you answer, keeping your voice tidy even if the kitchen is not.
			<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile">>
				"I was trying to make <<recipe_name $phase2 "article">>," you say. "I'll clear the glass."
			<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel")>>
				"I wanted to make <<recipe_name $phase2 "article">>," you say, looking more annoyed than sorry. "Bad place to leave a jar."
			<<else>>
				"I wanted to make <<recipe_name $phase2 "article">>," you say, letting the lie settle before Avery questions it.
			<</if>>
			<<if setup.foodstuff[$phase2]?.recipe>>
				If only you had any idea how to cook it.
				<br><br>
				"<<recipe_name $phase2 "cap">>?" Avery gives the kitchen another look. "That is a very convenient recipe to remember. <<if $avery_mansion.jobs.includes("kitchen")>>Clean up before you continue.<<else>>Try not to break anything else while experimenting.<</if>>
			<<else>>
				<br>
				"Makes sense," <<he>> answers, <<his>> curiosity satisfied. <<if $avery_mansion.jobs.includes("kitchen")>>"Just clean this up."<<else>>"Just be more careful."<</if>>
			<</if>>
			<br><br>
			<<averyKitchenExit "calm">>
		<</if>>
	<<case "white_wine" "red_wine">>
		<<if (_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "shy" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "polite" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant")>>
			"I wanted to pour myself some <<recipe_name $phase>>, but I knocked a jar off by accident," you explain. "I'm so sorry."<br>
		<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel")>>
			"Just wanted to drink some <<recipe_name $phase>>, but the jar was in my way," you shrug.<br>
		<<else>>
			"I wanted to pour myself some <<recipe_name $phase>>, but I knocked a jar off," you explain.<br>
		<</if>>
		<br>
		"Right," <<he>> sighs. "At least you didn't knock the wine bottles down. Still, if you want to drink, I have a collection of much better quality beverages. Those here are for cooking only. <<if $avery_mansion.jobs.includes("kitchen")>>Just clean this up.<<else>>Just be more careful.<</if>>"
		<br><br>
        <<averyKitchenExit "calm">>
	<<default>>
		<<if (_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "shy")>>
			"I was trying to make <<recipe_name $phase2 "article">>," you explain, glancing at the broken glass. "I panicked when you came in."
		<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant")>>
			"I was attempting <<recipe_name $phase2 "article">>," you say, smoothing your voice into something presentable.
		<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile">>
			"I was trying to make <<recipe_name $phase2 "article">>," you say. "I can clean the mess."
		<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel")>>
			"I wanted to make <<recipe_name $phase2 "article">>," you say, pushing confidence into the lie. "The jar slipped. Hardly my fault."
		<<else>>
			"I wanted to make <<recipe_name $phase2 "article">>," you say, watching Avery's face for the first crack in the excuse.
		<</if>>
		<<if setup.foodstuff[$phase2]?.recipe>>
			If only the excuse came with instructions.
			<br><br>
			"<<recipe_name $phase2 "cap">>?" Avery's eyebrow lifts. "You chose an ambitious moment to learn it. <<if $avery_mansion.jobs.includes("kitchen")>>Start by cleaning this mess.<<else>>Be more careful next time.<</if>>
		<<else>>
			<br>
			"Fine," <<he>> says, apparently willing to let the excuse stand. <<if $avery_mansion.jobs.includes("kitchen")>>Clean it before someone cuts themselves.<<else>>Do not make it worse.<</if>>
		<</if>>
		<br><br>
		<<averyKitchenExit "calm">>
	<</switch>>
	<br><br>
	<<icon "avery-kitchen.png">><<link [[Next|Mansion Kitchen]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<<else>>
	<<set $weekly.theft.avery_mansion.Ban to true>>
	You try to think of any excuse, <span class="red">but nothing comes to your mind.</span>
	<br><br>
	<<if $averyragerevealed is 1 and C.npc.Avery.rage gte random(20, 100)>>
		"So that's how it is?" Avery's eye twitches. "I take you in, provide for you, and you come here to steal from me to do what? Sell it yourself and get away from me?" <<He>> grabs your arm before you can retreat. "You have some nerve."<<garage>><<gtrauma>><<gstress>><<npcincr Avery rage 3>><<trauma 6>><<stress 6>>
		<br><br>
		<<link [[Next|Kitchen Steal Fight]]>><<set $fightstart to 1>><</link>>
	<<else>>
		"What's the matter?" Avery asks. "You have everything you need in my kitchen. So don't take it anywhere else, hm?<<if $avery_mansion.jobs.includes("kitchen")>> Clean it up.<</if>>"<<npcincr Avery rage 1>><<garage>>
		<br><br>
		<<averyKitchenExit "calm">>
		<br><br>
		<<icon "avery-kitchen.png">><<link [[Next|Mansion Kitchen]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
	<</if>>	
<</if>>

:: Mansion Steal Orphans
<<set $location to "avery_mansion">><<set $avery_passage to $passage>><<set $outside to 0>><<effects>><<avery_mansion>>
<<speechresolve>>
<<set $weekly.theft.avery_mansion.Ban to true>>
The broken glass leaves a sharp glitter across the kitchen tiles. You keep the <<recipe_name $phase "plural">> close, trying not to look as guilty as you feel.<br><br>
<<if (_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "shy")>>
	"I felt bad for the other orphans," you say quietly. "I thought I could share some. I wasn't trying to make trouble."
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant")>>
	"I meant to take it to the orphanage," you say, choosing your words with care. "Bailey never has enough, and I thought it might help."
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile">>
	"I wanted to give it to the orphans," you say at once. Your voice drops. "I'll put it back if you want me to."
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel")>>
	"Bailey's cheap," you say, chin lifting despite the mess. "I thought the orphans deserved better than whatever scraps they get."
<<else>>
	"I wanted to give it to the orphans," you say. "That's all."
<</if>>
<br><br>
Avery stares at you for a good while. For a moment, <<his>> anger catches on something softer. It does not last.<br><br>
<<if $averyragerevealed is 1 and C.npc.Avery.rage gte random(20, 100)>>
	"So that's how you're repaying me?" Avery's eye twitches. "I take you in, provide for you, and you come here to steal from me for people you barely even speak to?"<br><br>
	<<He>> steps closer, fingers closing around your arm. "After everything, you still try this."<<garage>><<gtrauma>><<gstress>><<npcincr Avery rage 3>><<trauma 6>><<stress 6>>
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Next|Kitchen Steal Fight]]>><<set $fightstart to 1>><</link>>
	<br>
<<else>>
	"So you wanted to steal from me. Great." Avery scoffs, but keeps <<himself>> under control. "Bailey feeds the orphans. This is my food. Put it down, and stop deciding who gets what from my kitchen."<<npcincr Avery rage 1>><<garage>>
	<br><br>
	<<averyKitchenExit "calm">>
	<br><br>
	<<icon "avery-kitchen.png">><<link [[Next|Mansion Kitchen]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<</if>>

:: Mansion Steal Admit
<<set $location to "avery_mansion">><<set $avery_passage to $passage>><<set $outside to 0>><<effects>><<avery_mansion>>
<<speechresolve>>
<<set $weekly.theft.avery_mansion.Ban to true>>
The excuse dies before it reaches your tongue. Avery waits, eyes fixed on the <<recipe_name $phase "plural">> and then on you.<br><br>
<<if (_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "shy")>>
	"I'm sorry," you mumble. "I was trying to steal from you."
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant")>>
	"I should be honest," you say, a little too carefully. "I was trying to take it without asking."
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile">>
	"I tried to steal it," you admit, shoulders sinking. "I'm sorry. Tell me what to do."
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel")>>
	"I might have been trying to steal from you," you say, though the broken jar makes the act hard to dress up.
<<else>>
	"I'm sorry," you say. "I tried to steal from you."
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<if $averyragerevealed is 1 and C.npc.Avery.rage gte random(20, 100)>>
	"So that's how it is?" Avery's eye twitches. "I take you in, provide for you, and you come here to steal from me. To do what? Sell it and get away from me?"<br><br>
	<<He>> closes the distance and catches your arm. "You really do have the nerve."<<garage>><<gtrauma>><<gstress>><<npcincr Avery rage 3>><<trauma 6>><<stress 6>>
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Next|Kitchen Steal Fight]]>><<set $fightstart to 1>><</link>>
	<br>
<<else>>
	"You did what?" Avery's tone sharpens. "No. Try again, and this time give me a reason before I decide you don't have one."<br><br>
	<<link [[Say you wanted to get a hidden food stash|Mansion Steal Stash Calm]]>><</link>><br>
	<<if (effectiveTransformationLevel("fox") gte 6) and $phase is "chicken_egg">>
		<<link [[Say you wanted to bury the egg|Mansion Steal Bury Egg]]>><</link>><br>
	<</if>>
	<<if ($avery_mansion.kitchen_stock && Array.isArray($avery_mansion.kitchen_stock.requested) && $avery_mansion.kitchen_stock.requested.includes($phase))>>
		<<link [[Say you wanted to save it for another time|Mansion Steal Save]]>><</link>><br>
	<<else>>
		<<link [[Say you wanted to save it for another time|Mansion Steal Save Fail]]>><</link>><br>
	<</if>>
	<<if $phase is "pork" or $phase is "beef">>
		<<if ((effectiveTransformationLevel("wolf") gte 6) or (effectiveTransformationLevel("bird") gte 6) or (effectiveTransformationLevel("cat") gte 6) or (effectiveTransformationLevel("bear") gte 6) or (effectiveTransformationLevel("fox") gte 6))>>
			<<link [[Say you wanted to eat <<recipe_name $phase "article">>|Mansion Steal Raw]]>><</link>><br>
		<</if>>
		<<if Object.values($children).find(child => child.mother === "pc" && child.location === "wolf_cave")>>
			<<link [[Say you wanted to feed it to a child|Mansion Steal Child]]>><</link>><br>
		<</if>>
		<<if $syndromewolves gte 1>>
			<<link [[Say you wanted to give it to Black Wolf|Mansion Steal Friend]]>><<set $phase2 to "wolf">><</link>><br>
		<</if>>
		<<if $syndromebird gte 1>>
			<<link [[Say you wanted to give it to the Great Hawk|Mansion Steal Friend]]>><<set $phase2 to "bird">><</link>><br>
		<</if>>
	<</if>>
	<<if (effectiveTransformationLevel("bear") gte 6) and $phase is "wild_honeycomb">>
		<<link [[Say you like honey|Mansion Steal Honey]]>><</link>><br>
	<</if>>
	<<link [[Say you wanted to give it to the orphans|Mansion Steal Orphans]]>><</link>><br>
<</if>>

:: Mansion Steal Cooking Calm
<<set $location to "avery_mansion">><<set $avery_passage to $passage>><<set $outside to 0>><<effects>><<avery_mansion>>
<<speechresolve>>
<<set $skulduggerydifficulty to 400>><<skulduggerycheck "silent">>
<<if $skulduggerysuccess is 1>>
	<<if (_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "shy")>>
		"I was trying to cook <<recipe_name $phase2 "article">>," you say, glancing at the scattered glass. "I thought I could manage it."
	<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant")>>
		"I was attempting <<recipe_name $phase2 "article">>," you say, smoothing your voice into something respectable. "The kitchen got away from me."
	<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile">>
		"I was trying to make <<recipe_name $phase2 "article">>," you say at once. "I can clean it up."
	<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel")>>
		"I was making <<recipe_name $phase2 "article">>," you say, like the broken jar is the kitchen's fault. "Obviously."
	<<else>>
		"I wanted to cook <<recipe_name $phase2 "article">>," you answer, trying to sound as if you had not invented the excuse two seconds ago.
	<</if>>
	<br><br>
	Avery raises <<his>> eyebrow. <<He>> looks from you, to the <<recipe_name $phase "plural">>, then back to you.<br><br>
	"<<recipe_name $phase2 "cap">>? There aren't any <<recipe_name $phase "plural">> in <<recipe_name $phase2 "article">>." <<His>> suspicion settles in the silence after the words.<br><br>
	<<link [[Say you're experimenting|Mansion Steal Cooking Calm Lie]]>><</link>><br>
	<<link [[Admit to lying|Mansion Steal Cooking Calm Truth]]>><</link>>
<<else>>
	"I wanted to cook... <<recipe_name $phase2 "article">>?" you say, grabbing the first thing that sounds plausible.<br><br>
	Avery raises <<his>> eyebrow, then smirks. "<<recipe_name $phase2 "cap">>? I didn't know you knew that one." <<He>> lets the silence stretch just long enough to make you regret speaking. "Alright. Change of plans. <span class="pink">Make <<recipe_name $phase2 "article">> instead of <<recipe_name $avery_mansion.food "article">></span>."
	<<if $avery_mansion.jobs.includes("kitchen")>>
		<br><br>"And don't forget to clean the kitchen afterwards."
	<</if>>
	<br><br>
	<<averyKitchenExit "calm">><<if $avery_mansion.schedule is "dinner">> You will have to come back to it later. For now, Avery is hungry.<<else>> You are in trouble.<</if>>
	<br><br>
	<<icon "avery-kitchen.png">><<link [[Next|Mansion Kitchen]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<</if>>

:: Mansion Steal Cooking Calm Lie
<<set $location to "avery_mansion">><<set $avery_passage to $passage>><<set $outside to 0>><<effects>><<avery_mansion>>
<<speechresolve>>
<<set $skulduggerydifficulty to 800>><<skulduggerycheck "silent">>
<<if $skulduggerysuccess is 1>>
	<<if (_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "shy")>>
		"I wanted to try something new," you say. "Only a little. I thought it might work."
	<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant")>>
		"It was an experiment," you say, giving the broken jar a small, apologetic look. "Not a very graceful one, clearly."
	<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile">>
		"I was experimenting," you say. "I'll stop if you want me to."
	<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel")>>
		"I'm experimenting," you answer. "That's how cooking improves."
	<<else>>
		"I'm experimenting," you answer, making yourself sound more certain than you feel.
	<</if>>
	<br><br>
	<<if $housekeeping gte 200>>
		Avery studies your face for a moment before <<his>> frown eases. "Obviously you are. You're a <<if $housekeeping gte 600>>great<<else>>good<</if>> cook.<<if $avery_mansion.jobs.includes("kitchen")>> Just remember to clean up the mess when you're done.<</if>>"
	<<else>>
		Avery sighs. "Don't. You're not exactly the most experienced cook. Stick to the recipes, at least for now.<<if $avery_mansion.jobs.includes("kitchen")>> And clean up the mess when you're done.<</if>>"
	<</if>>
<<else>>
	"I was thinking about mixing some <<recipe_name $phase>> with <<recipe_name $phase2>>, yes," you say. It sounds worse once it is out loud.<br><br>
	"Stop lying to me," Avery says with a frown. "I expect better from you.<<if $avery_mansion.jobs.includes("kitchen")>> Now clean it up.<</if>>"<<llove>><<npcincr Avery love -1>>
	<<set $weekly.theft.avery_mansion.Ban to true>>
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<averyKitchenExit "calm">>
<br><br>
<<icon "avery-kitchen.png">><<link [[Next|Mansion Kitchen]]>><<endevent>><</link>>

:: Mansion Steal Cooking Calm Truth
<<set $location to "avery_mansion">><<set $avery_passage to $passage>><<set $outside to 0>><<effects>><<avery_mansion>>
<<speechresolve>>
<<if (_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "shy")>>
	"I'm sorry. I lied," you admit, words bunching together. "I was hoping it would sound like a good excuse."
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant")>>
	"That was not true," you say. "I was trying to make it sound better than it was."
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile">>
	"I lied," you admit immediately. "I wasn't going to cook anything."
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel")>>
	"Fine. I lied," you say. "I needed an excuse and picked a bad one."
<<else>>
	"I lied," you admit. "I wasn't planning to cook anything. It was just an excuse."
<</if>>
<br><br>
"An excuse for what?" Avery asks, <<his>> voice sharpening. <<He>> still seems willing to hear you out, but only just.<br><br>
<<link [[Say you wanted to get a hidden food stash|Mansion Steal Stash Calm]]>><</link>><br>
<<if (effectiveTransformationLevel("fox") gte 6) and $phase is "chicken_egg">>
	<<link [[Say you wanted to bury the egg|Mansion Steal Bury Egg]]>><</link>><br>
<</if>>
<<if ($avery_mansion.kitchen_stock && Array.isArray($avery_mansion.kitchen_stock.requested) && $avery_mansion.kitchen_stock.requested.includes($phase))>>
	<<link [[Say you wanted to save it for another time|Mansion Steal Save]]>><</link>><br>
<<else>>
	<<link [[Say you wanted to save it for another time|Mansion Steal Save Fail]]>><</link>><br>
<</if>>
<<if $phase is "pork" or $phase is "beef">>
	<<if ((effectiveTransformationLevel("wolf") gte 6) or (effectiveTransformationLevel("bird") gte 6) or (effectiveTransformationLevel("cat") gte 6) or (effectiveTransformationLevel("bear") gte 6) or (effectiveTransformationLevel("fox") gte 6))>>
		<<link [[Say you wanted to eat <<recipe_name $phase "article">>|Mansion Steal Raw]]>><</link>><br>
	<</if>>
	<<if Object.values($children).find(child => child.mother === "pc" && child.location === "wolf_cave")>>
		<<link [[Say you wanted to feed it to a child|Mansion Steal Child]]>><</link>><br>
	<</if>>
	<<if $syndromewolves gte 1>>
		<<link [[Say you wanted to give it to Black Wolf|Mansion Steal Friend]]>><<set $phase2 to "wolf">><</link>><br>
	<</if>>
	<<if $syndromebird gte 1>>
		<<link [[Say you wanted to give it to the Great Hawk|Mansion Steal Friend]]>><<set $phase2 to "bird">><</link>><br>
	<</if>>
<</if>>
<<if (effectiveTransformationLevel("bear") gte 6) and $phase is "wild_honeycomb">>
	<<link [[Say you like honey|Mansion Steal Honey]]>><</link>><br>
<</if>>
<<link [[Say you're making a surprise|Mansion Steal Surprise]]>><</link>><br>
<<link [[Say you wanted to give it to the orphans|Mansion Steal Orphans]]>><</link>><br>
<<if effectiveTransformationLevel("fox") gte 2 and $phase is "chicken_egg">>
	<<link [[Defend stealing as your natural need|Mansion Steal Fox]]>><</link>><br>
<<else>>
	<<link [[Admit to stealing|Mansion Steal Admit 2]]>><</link>><br>
<</if>>

:: Mansion Steal Bury Egg
<<set $location to "avery_mansion">><<set $avery_passage to $passage>><<set $outside to 0>><<effects>><<avery_mansion>>
<<speechresolve>>
<<if (_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "shy")>>
	"I'm sorry. I wanted to bury the egg," you say, cradling it close. "I'm a fox<<girl>>, and it felt important."
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant")>>
	"This will sound ridiculous," you say, "but I wanted to bury the egg. Fox instincts, I think."
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile">>
	"I wanted to bury it," you answer at once. "I can put it back if you tell me to."
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel")>>
	"I'm a fox<<girl>>," you say. "Foxes hide food. The egg was getting hidden."
<<else>>
	"I wanted to bury the egg," you say. "I'm a fox<<girl>>, it's a natural need."
<</if>>
<br><br>
Avery looks between you and the egg. <<His>> mouth twitches despite the broken glass.
<br><br>
"You wanted to bury it. Obviously." <<He>> sighs. "I suppose you do look the part.<<if $avery_mansion.jobs.includes("kitchen")>> Clean this up, my <<= $player.gender_appearance is "m" ? "kit" : "vixen">>. Then take the egg and don't make another mess.<<else>> Leave the mess for the maids. Take the egg and don't make another mess.<</if>>"<<garage>><<npcincr Avery rage 1>><<tending_pick $phase 1 1>>
<br><br>
<<averyKitchenExit "calm">>
<br><br>
<<icon "avery-kitchen.png">><<link [[Next|Mansion Kitchen]]>><<endevent>><</link>>

:: Mansion Steal Save
<<set $location to "avery_mansion">><<set $avery_passage to $passage>><<set $outside to 0>><<effects>><<avery_mansion>>
<<speechresolve>>
<<if (_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "shy")>>
	"I thought I'd need <<recipe_name $phase "plural">> for cooking later," you say. "I didn't want you to worry about stocking more."
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant")>>
	"I noticed the kitchen stock changes often," you say. "I thought saving the <<recipe_name $phase "plural">> would help with later meals."
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile">>
	"I wanted to save it for later," you say. "I thought it was useful."
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel")>>
	"You only keep so much stocked," you say. "I was saving the <<recipe_name $phase "plural">> before they disappeared."
<<else>>
	"I wanted to keep it for later," you say. "I'll need <<recipe_name $phase "plural">> for cooking."
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<if $avery_mansion.kitchen_stock.requested.length gte 3>>
	<<set $avery_mansion.kitchen_stock.requested.pushUnique($phase)>>
	<<set _removed_ingredient to $avery_mansion.kitchen_stock.requested.shift()>>
	Avery follows your gaze to the shelves, then lets out a quiet sigh. "Right. I'll keep that in mind. I'll get rid of <<recipe_name _removed_ingredient "plural">> instead."
<<else>>
	Avery's frown deepens. "I wouldn't have got rid of that. The next to go are <<recipe_name $avery_mansion.kitchen_stock.requested.shift() "plural">>."
<</if>>
<br><br>
"Leave the <<recipe_name $phase "plural">>. I'm not taking it anywhere. And <<if $avery_mansion.jobs.includes("kitchen")>>clean up this mess.<<else>>don't make another mess.<</if>>"
<br><br>
<<averyKitchenExit "calm">><<if $avery_mansion.schedule is "dinner">> Dinner will have to wait. Avery is hungry.<</if>>
<br><br>
<<icon "avery-kitchen.png">><<link [[Next|Mansion Kitchen]]>><<endevent>><</link>>

