	<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant")>>
		"I was attempting <<recipe_name $phase2 "article">>," you say, but the polite shape of the sentence cannot hide the lie.
	<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile">>
		"I was making <<recipe_name $phase2 "article">>," you say. "I can clean it."
	<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel")>>
		"I was cooking <<recipe_name $phase2 "article">>," you say. "What does it look like?"
	<<else>>
		"I wanted to cook <<recipe_name $phase2 "article">>," you answer quickly, as if speed can make it true.
	<</if>>
	<br><br>
	Avery takes a step towards you. "You thought I wouldn't know you were lying? I'll show you what I do to liars."<<garage>><<gtrauma>><<gstress>><<npcincr Avery rage 3>><<trauma 6>><<stress 6>>
<<else>>
	"I was going to cook... <<recipe_name $phase2 "article">>," you say, choosing the first recipe that sounds plausible.
    <br><br>
	Avery takes a step towards you. "So that's how it is. Not only will you lie to my face, you'll do it badly. I'll show you what I do to liars."<<garage>><<gtrauma>><<gstress>><<npcincr Avery rage 3>><<trauma 6>><<stress 6>>
