:: Mansion Steal Honey Rage
<<set $location to "avery_mansion">><<set $avery_passage to $passage>><<set $outside to 0>><<effects>><<avery_mansion>>
<<speechresolve>>
"I really like honey."
<br><br>
"It's a honeycomb, not honey," Avery snaps.
<br><br>
<<if (_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "shy")>>
	"I like it from the source," you answer almost automatically, your animalistic nature taking over for a moment.
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant")>>
	"Fresh from the source has its own appeal," you say, and immediately wish you had said it less neatly.
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile">>
	"It's better like this," you say. "Sorry."
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel")>>
	"It's better fresh from the source," you answer. "You asked."
<<else>>
	"It's better fresh from the source," you answer automatically, your animalistic nature taking over for a moment.
<</if>>
<br><br>
Avery stares at you for a moment, then grimaces. "That's disgusting. Just make honey with it.<<if $avery_mansion.jobs.includes("kitchen")>> And clean it up.<</if>>"
<br><br>
<<averyKitchenExit "rage">><<averyKitchenPillConsequence>>
<br><br>
<<icon "avery-kitchen.png">><<link [[Next|Mansion Kitchen]]>><<endevent>><</link>>

:: Mansion Steal Surprise Rage
<<set $location to "avery_mansion">><<set $avery_passage to $passage>><<set $outside to 0>><<effects>><<avery_mansion>>
<<speechresolve>>
<<if (_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "shy" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "polite" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant")>>
	"But if I tell you, the surprise will be spoiled..."
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel")>>
	"Can't tell you. It'll ruin the surprise."
<<else>>
	"I wanted to make you a surprise!"
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<switch $phase>>
<<case "beef">>
	"A surprise?" Avery's expression softens. It seems <<he>> has something on <<his>> mind. "I might excuse your clumsiness if you're making what I'm thinking."
<<case "pasta">>
	"A surprise?" Avery's anger loosens a little. "<<if !Array.isArray($foodstuff.linguine?.knownFavorite)>>It had better be worth the broken jar.<<else>>If this is linguine, I might forgive the mess.<</if>>"
<<case "sugar">>
	"A surprise?" Avery raises <<his>> eyebrow, <<his>> expression softening slightly. "Making me dessert? It had better be worth the mess you've made."
<<case "flour">>
	"A surprise?" Avery raises <<his>> eyebrow, <<his>> expression softening slightly. "Are you baking me something? It had better be worth the mess you've made."
<<default>>
	"A surprise?" Avery's eyebrow lifts, suspicion giving way to interest. "For your sake, it had better be good."
<</switch>>
<br><br>
<<if $avery_mansion.jobs.includes("kitchen")>>
	"Clean it up first."
<</if>>
<<averyKitchenExit "rage">><<averyKitchenPillConsequence>>
<br><br>
<<icon "avery-kitchen.png">><<link [[Next|Mansion Kitchen]]>><<endevent>><</link>>

:: Mansion Steal Dumb Rage
<<set $location to "avery_mansion">><<set $avery_passage to $passage>><<set $outside to 0>><<effects>><<avery_mansion>>
<<speechresolve>>
<<set $skulduggerydifficulty to 1200>>
<<if ($phase is "bottle_of_milk" and (effectiveTransformationLevel("cat") gte 6)) or ($phase is "wild_honeycomb" and (effectiveTransformationLevel("bear") gte 6)) or ($phase is "chicken_egg" and (effectiveTransformationLevel("fox") gte 6)) or ($phase is "pork" and (effectiveTransformationLevel("cow") gte 6))>>
	<<set $skulduggerydifficulty to 800>>
<</if>>
<<skulduggerycheck "silent">>
<<if $skulduggerysuccess is 1>>
	<<switch $phase>>
	<<case "banana" "wild_carrot" "chilli_pepper">>
		<<if (_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "shy" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "polite" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant")>>
			"I wanted to use <<recipe_name $phase "article">>," you say the first thing that comes to mind. "F-for pleasure."<br>
		<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel")>>
			"I wanted to fuck <<recipe_name $phase "article">>," you say, because subtlety already died with the jar.<br>
		<<else>>
			"I wanted to use <<recipe_name $phase "article">> as a dildo," you say, choosing the first excuse shameless enough to work.<br>
		<</if>>
        <br>
		Avery frowns. "Careful. Or I'll put it in you myself.<<if $avery_mansion.jobs.includes("kitchen")>> Clean this mess up.<</if>>"
		<br><br>
		<<averyKitchenExit "rage">><<averyKitchenPillConsequence>>
	<<case "bottle_of_milk">>
		<<if (effectiveTransformationLevel("cat") gte 6)>>
			You meow and drink the milk without saying a word. Avery raises <<his>> eyebrow, but doesn't say anything until you finish.
            <br><br>
			"That's it? That's all you wanted to do? <<He>> scoffs. Well, you are a cat.<<if $avery_mansion.jobs.includes("kitchen")>> Clean this mess up.<</if>>"
		<<else>>
			<<if (_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "shy")>>
				"I was trying to make <<recipe_name $phase2 "article">>," you explain, trying to sound small rather than guilty. "The crash made me panic."
			<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant")>>
				"I was attempting <<recipe_name $phase2 "article">>," you say, as if manners can make the broken glass less obvious.
			<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile">>
				"I was trying to make <<recipe_name $phase2 "article">>," you say. "I'll tidy it before anyone steps on it."
			<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel")>>
				"I wanted to make <<recipe_name $phase2 "article">>," you say, before Avery can call it theft. "The jar picked a bad time to fall."
			<<else>>
				"I wanted to make <<recipe_name $phase2 "article">>," you say, trying not to add too many details.
			<</if>>
			<<if setup.foodstuff[$phase2]?.recipe>>
				If only your confidence matched your cooking knowledge.
                <br><br>
				"<<recipe_name $phase2 "cap">>?" Avery raises <<his>> eyebrow. "I didn't know you could cook <<recipe_name $phase2 "article">>. So you are good at something. <<if $avery_mansion.jobs.includes("kitchen")>>Clean it up.<<else>>Don't let me catch you breaking anything again.<</if>>"
			<<else>>
				<br><br>
				"Hm, makes sense," <<he>> steps away from the doorframe.
				<<if $avery_mansion.jobs.includes("kitchen")>>
					"Clean it up. 
				<<else>>
					"Leave it for the maid to clean. 
				<</if>>
				And don't make another mess. <<if $avery_mansion.schedule is "dinner">>I'll be waiting in the dining room.<</if>>"
			<</if>>
		<</if>>
		<br><br>
		<<averyKitchenExit "rage">><<averyKitchenPillConsequence>>
	<<case "apple" "orange" "lemon" "pear" "strawberry" "peach" "plum" "blackberry" "tomato">>
		<<if (_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "shy" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "polite" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant")>>
			"I wanted a snack," you say, glancing at the fruit in your hand. "I knocked the jar down trying to get it."
		<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel")>>
			"I wanted something fresh," you say, chin lifting despite the glass around your feet. "Bad shelf, worse jar."
		<<else>>
			"I wanted something fresh," you say. "I reached too quickly, and the jar went over."
		<</if>>
        <br><br>
		"Right, of course. <<if $avery_mansion.jobs.includes("kitchen")>>Just clean this up.<<else>>Just be more careful.<</if>>"
        <br><br>
		<<averyKitchenExit "rage">><<averyKitchenPillConsequence>>
	<<case "wild_honeycomb">>
		<<if (effectiveTransformationLevel("bear") gte 6)>>
			<<if (_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "shy" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "polite" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant")>>
				"I wanted the honeycomb," you say. "The wax too. And the larvae," which is apparently where Avery decides <<he>> has heard enough.<br>
			<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel")>>
				"I'm a bear<<girl>>," you say. "Honeycomb means wax, larvae, the good bits," and Avery cuts you off before you can keep listing them.<br>
			<<else>>
				"I like honeycombs whole," you say. "Wax, honey, larvae," and Avery interrupts with a look that says that was already too much.<br>
			<</if>>
            <br>
			"I understand. You don't need to get into the details, I don't want to know it.<<if $avery_mansion.jobs.includes("kitchen")>> Just clean up the mess after yourself.<</if>>"
		<<else>>
			<<if (_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "shy" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "polite" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant")>>
				"I thought I could use the wax for candles," you explain. "Then the jar slipped. I'm sorry."<br>
			<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel")>>
				"Candles," you say, as if the answer is obvious. "Honey-scented ones. Very classy."<br>
			<<else>>
				"I wanted the wax for candles," you explain. "The honey was not the point."<br>
			<</if>>
            <br>
			"Candles?" Avery raises <<his>> eyebrow, slightly surprised. "I didn't know you were interested in such things. Well, just make sure it does not go to waste. They are hard to come by.<<if $avery_mansion.jobs.includes("kitchen")>> And also, clean that mess before somebody gets injured.<</if>>"
		<</if>>
        <br><br>
		<<averyKitchenExit "rage">><<averyKitchenPillConsequence>>
	<<case "garlic_bulb">>
		<<if (_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "shy" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "polite" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant")>>
			"I think I'm coming down with something," you start. "I thought garlic might help before it got worse."<br>
		<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel")>>
			"My throat feels awful," you say. "Garlic seemed worth a try."<br>
		<<else>>
			"My throat is sore," you start. "I thought garlic might stop it early. Better than coughing over your kitchen."<br>
		<</if>>
        <br>
		"How considerate.<<if $avery_mansion.jobs.includes("kitchen")>> Sweep the glass before you medicate yourself.<</if>>"
        <<averyKitchenExit "rage">>
	<<case "chicken_egg">>
		<<if (effectiveTransformationLevel("fox") gte 6)>>
			<<if (_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "shy" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "polite" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant")>>
				"I wanted to bury it," you admit. "Fox<<girl>> instincts. It sounded sensible until you walked in."<br>
			<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel")>>
				"Fox<<girl>> instincts," you say. "Egg, hole, done. You interrupted the plan."<br>
			<<else>>
				"I wanted to bury the egg," you explain. "It felt like the fox<<girl>> thing to do."<br>
			<</if>>
            <br>
			Avery stares at you for a moment, then laughs under <<his>> breath. "Of course you did. You do look the part.
			<<if $avery_mansion.jobs.includes("kitchen")>>
				You still have to clean it, my <<= $player.gender_appearance is "m" ? "kit" : "vixen">>." <<He>> sighs. "Take the egg before I change my mind.
			<<else>>
				Leave that for the maids." <<He>> stops, then sighs. "Take the egg, and do not turn this into a habit.
			<</if>>
			"<br><br>
			<<He>> leaves the kitchen.<<tending_pick $phase 1 1>>
		<<else>>
			<<if (_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "shy")>>
				"I was trying to make <<recipe_name $phase2 "article">>," you say, your attention fixed on the mess. "I startled when you came in."
			<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant")>>
				"I was attempting <<recipe_name $phase2 "article">>," you say, setting your voice straight while the floor betrays you.
			<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile">>
				"I was trying to make <<recipe_name $phase2 "article">>," you say. "I'll fix the kitchen."
			<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel")>>
				"I wanted to make <<recipe_name $phase2 "article">>," you say, wearing the excuse like armour. "That jar was asking for it."
			<<else>>
				"I wanted to make <<recipe_name $phase2 "article">>," you say, hoping plain confidence will do the work for you.
			<</if>>
			<<if setup.foodstuff[$phase2]?.recipe>>
				If only Avery asked for details you could answer.
				<br><br>
				"<<recipe_name $phase2 "cap">>?" Avery raises <<his>> eyebrow. "I didn't know you could cook <<recipe_name $phase2 "article">>. So you are good at something. <<if $avery_mansion.jobs.includes("kitchen")>>Clean it up.<<else>>Don't let me catch you breaking anything again.<</if>>
			<<else>>
				<br><br>
				"Fine. That almost makes sense," <<he>> says, moving aside.
				<<if $avery_mansion.jobs.includes("kitchen")>>
					"Clean it up. 
				<<else>>
					"Leave it for the maid to clean. 
				<</if>>
				And leave the rest of the kitchen alone. <<if $avery_mansion.schedule is "dinner">>I'll be waiting in the dining room.<</if>>"
			<</if>>
		<</if>>
		<br><br>
		<<averyKitchenExit "rage">><<averyKitchenPillConsequence>>
	<<case "beef" "pork">>
		<<if (effectiveTransformationLevel("cow") gte 6) and $phase is "pork">>
			<<if (_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "shy" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "polite" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant")>>
				"I'm sorry," you say. "Seeing it in the fridge felt wrong, and I don't know why." The quiet moo afterwards does more explaining than you meant it to.<br>
			<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel")>>
				You let out a low, stubborn moo. More bull than obedient cow. "It's pork. That is disgusting for me now, so I got rid of it."<br>
			<<else>>
				"I did not like seeing it in the fridge," you say. A soft moo slips out before you can stop it.<br>
			<</if>>
            <br>
			"That's all? You felt bad about some meat in the fridge and decided to steal it from me?" <<He>> frowns. "I'll overlook it but only this once. Put it down.
			<<if $avery_mansion.jobs.includes("kitchen")>> And clean that up.<<else>> And don't make another mess.<</if>>"<br>
			<br>
			<<averyKitchenExit "rage">><<averyKitchenPillConsequence>>
		<<elseif ((effectiveTransformationLevel("wolf") gte 6) or (effectiveTransformationLevel("bird") gte 6) or (effectiveTransformationLevel("cat") gte 6) or (effectiveTransformationLevel("bear") gte 6) or (effectiveTransformationLevel("fox") gte 6))>>
			<<if (_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "shy" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "polite" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant")>>
				"I wanted raw meat," you start, then gesture weakly at yourself. "I'm a <<if (effectiveTransformationLevel("cat") gte 6)>>cat<<girl>><<elseif (effectiveTransformationLevel("wolf") gte 6)>>wolf<<girl>><<elseif (effectiveTransformationLevel("bear") gte 6)>>bear<<girl>><<elseif (effectiveTransformationLevel("fox") gte 6)>>fox<<girl>><<elseif (effectiveTransformationLevel("bird") gte 6)>>harpy<</if>>. It made sense in the moment."<br>
			<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel")>>
				"I'm a <<if (effectiveTransformationLevel("cat") gte 6)>>cat<<girl>><<elseif (effectiveTransformationLevel("wolf") gte 6)>>wolf<<girl>><<elseif (effectiveTransformationLevel("bear") gte 6)>>bear<<girl>><<elseif (effectiveTransformationLevel("fox") gte 6)>>fox<<girl>><<elseif (effectiveTransformationLevel("bird") gte 6)>>harpy<</if>>, so yes, I took raw meat. Call it instinct, if that makes you happier."<br>
			<<else>>
				"I craved raw meat," you start your explanation. "I'm a <<if (effectiveTransformationLevel("cat") gte 6)>>cat<<girl>><<elseif (effectiveTransformationLevel("wolf") gte 6)>>wolf<<girl>><<elseif (effectiveTransformationLevel("bear") gte 6)>>bear<<girl>><<elseif (effectiveTransformationLevel("fox") gte 6)>>fox<<girl>><<elseif (effectiveTransformationLevel("bird") gte 6)>>harpy<</if>>. My instincts wanted meat before manners could get involved."<br>
			<</if>>
			<br>
			"It's disgusting. <<if $avery_mansion.jobs.includes("kitchen")>>Clean up the mess up and put the <<recipe_name $phase2>> down.<<else>>Put the <<recipe_name $phase2>> down, and don't do it again.<</if>>"
			<br><br>
            <<averyKitchenExit "rage">><<if $avery_mansion.jobs.includes("kitchen")>>Avery didn't mention it, but you probably still have to clean that kitchen.<</if>>
		<<else>>
			<<if (_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "shy")>>
				"I was trying to make <<recipe_name $phase2 "article">>," you explain, swallowing before Avery can interrupt. "I panicked after the jar fell."
			<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant")>>
				"I was attempting <<recipe_name $phase2 "article">>," you answer, clipped and careful over the mess at your feet.
			<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile">>
				"I was trying to make <<recipe_name $phase2 "article">>," you say. "I'll sweep it up."
			<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel")>>
				"I wanted to make <<recipe_name $phase2 "article">>," you say, refusing to let the mess shame you. "Maybe stock sturdier jars."
			<<else>>
				"I wanted to make <<recipe_name $phase2 "article">>," you say, choosing the shortest version of the lie.
			<</if>>
			<<if setup.foodstuff[$phase2]?.recipe>>
				If only naming the dish meant you could prepare it.
				<br><br>
				"<<recipe_name $phase2 "cap">>?" Avery looks from you to the mess. "You picked a bold recipe for someone surrounded by broken glass. <<if $avery_mansion.jobs.includes("kitchen")>>Clean it up.<<else>>Do not let me catch another crash.<</if>>"
			<<else>>
				<br><br>
				"I suppose that explains it," <<he>> says, no longer blocking the way.
				<<if $avery_mansion.jobs.includes("kitchen")>>
					"Clean it up. 
				<<else>>
					"Leave it for the maid to clean. 
				<</if>>
				And don't make another mess."
			<</if>>
            <br><br>
			<<averyKitchenExit "rage">><<averyKitchenPillConsequence>>
		<</if>>
	<<case "white_wine" "red_wine">>
		<<if (_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "shy" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "polite" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant")>>
			"I wanted some <<recipe_name $phase>>," you explain. "The jar caught my hand, then it was on the floor."<br>
		<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel")>>
			"I wanted a drink," you say with a shrug. "The jar made it dramatic."<br>
		<<else>>
			"I was pouring <<recipe_name $phase>>," you explain. "Then I clipped the jar."<br>
		<</if>>
		<br>
		"Aren't you desperate? There are for cooking-only. <<if $avery_mansion.jobs.includes("kitchen")>>Clean this mess up.<<else>>Don't break anything else.<</if>>"
		<br><br>
        <<averyKitchenExit "rage">><<averyKitchenPillConsequence>>
	<<default>>
		<<if (_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "shy")>>
			"I was trying to make <<recipe_name $phase2 "article">>," you explain, looking past Avery to the glass. "The crash made me panic."
		<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant")>>
			"I was attempting <<recipe_name $phase2 "article">>," you say, speaking as neatly as possible over the smashed jar.
		<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile">>
			"I was trying to make <<recipe_name $phase2 "article">>," you say. "I'll deal with it."
		<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel")>>
			"I wanted to make <<recipe_name $phase2 "article">>," you say, meeting Avery's stare. "The jar was already a problem."
		<<else>>
			"I wanted to make <<recipe_name $phase2 "article">>," you say, keeping your voice level while Avery studies the floor.
		<</if>>
		<<if setup.foodstuff[$phase2]?.recipe>>
			If only the kitchen believed you.
			<br><br>
			"<<recipe_name $phase2 "cap">>?" Avery's mouth tightens. "Fine. Pretend this was cooking. <<if $avery_mansion.jobs.includes("kitchen")>>Clean it up.<<else>>Break anything else and I will not be so patient.<</if>>"
		<<else>>
			<br><br>
			"Right," <<he>> says at last, stepping back from the doorframe.
			<<if $avery_mansion.jobs.includes("kitchen")>>
				"Clean it up. 
			<<else>>
				"Leave it for the maid to clean. 
			<</if>>
			And don't make another mess."
		<</if>>
        <br><br>
		<<averyKitchenExit "rage">><<averyKitchenPillConsequence>>
	<</switch>>
	<br><br>
	<<icon "avery-kitchen.png">><<link [[Next|Mansion Kitchen]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<<else>>
	You search for a useful excuse, <span class="red">but your thoughts go completely blank.</span>
	<br><br>
	"So that's what this is?" Avery's eye twitches. "I let you into my home, and you use my kitchen like a market stall?" <<He>> seizes your arm. "Unbelievable."<<garage>><<gtrauma>><<gstress>><<npcincr Avery rage 3>><<trauma 6>><<stress 6>>
	<br><br>
	<<set $weekly.theft.avery_mansion.Ban to true>>
	<<link [[Next|Kitchen Steal Fight]]>><<set $fightstart to 1>><</link>>
